h information as triplets or paths [38], and molecule graphs consist of higher-order structures (e.g., cellular complexes) [26], as shown"},{"id":"c34","chunkId":"743155d9b0541c99_c_63534c0e7dcbf97a","docId":"743155d9b0541c99","docTitle":"2401.15391_MultiHop_RAG_Benchmarking_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Multi_Hop","page":3,"quote":"Each doc- ument within this corpus, represented as di ∈D, is segmented into a set of chunks.These chunks are then transformed into vector representations using an embedding model and stored in an embedding database."},{"id":"c35","chunkId":"8bbe93a93b05967d_c_ac7298f01655cdf6","docId":"8bbe93a93b05967d","docTitle":"2410.13070_Is_Semantic_Chunking_Worth_the_Computational_Cost","page":1,"quote":"1 Introduction In Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) sys- tems, cutting documents into smaller units called “chunks”"},{"id":"c36","chunkId":"ac529ab762fd1672_c_63366a50187da7c6","docId":"ac529ab762fd1672","docTitle":"HybridRAG: Integrating Knowledge Graphs and Vector Retrieval Augmented Generation for Efficient Information Extraction","page":2,"quote":"In traditional VectorRAG, the given external documents are di- vided into multiple chunks because of the limitation of context size of the language model."},{"id":"c37","chunkId":"bd72eebf611df136_c_fa36d8940617e6c5","docId":"bd72eebf611df136","docTitle":"2410.05779_LightRAG_Simple_and_Fast_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation","page":2,"quote":"Original Chunks ID: xxx Source: Honey Bee Target: Industrial agriculture Keywords: Agriculture ..."},{"id":"c38","chunkId":"d9eaa1398abac0df_c_54a9bcb91e94bb8d","docId":"d9eaa1398abac0df","docTitle":"2310.11511_Self_RAG_Learning_to_Retrieve_Generate_and_Critique_through_Self_Refle","page":5,"quote":"During training, we mask out the retrieved text chunks (surrounded by <p> and </p> in Figure 2) for loss calculation and expand the original vocabulary V with a set of reflection tokens { Critique , Retrieve }."}],"mastery":null}},{"type":"NotesGraph","id":"note